:m The `name_index` function generates an inverted index where keys are word tokens derived from Unicode character names, and values are sets of characters that have those words in their names. It uses a generator expression to efficiently process and map each character within a given range.
```python
from collections.abc import Iterator
def name_index(start: int = 32, end: int = sys.maxunicode + 1) -> dict[str, set[str]]:
index: dict[str, set[str]] = {}
for char in (chr(i) for i in range(start, end)):
if name := unicodedata.name(char, ''):
for word in tokenize(name):
index.setdefault(word, set()).add(char)
return index
```

