:m In Python, `list` is considered generic because it can hold elements of any type. In contrast, before Java 1.5, all collections could only store objects of the `Object` class, making them specific in a way that they allowed no other types.
Java introduced generics with version 1.5 to provide more flexibility by allowing collection types to be parameterized with specific types at compile time:
```java
