:m Logical coupling pertains to the way code interacts based on the structure and design of classes, while physical coupling deals with actual code dependencies like headers, libraries, and file inclusions. Logical coupling can be managed through design patterns and interfaces, whereas physical coupling often arises due to direct imports or function calls.
For example:
