:m Variation points are specific areas of the code where changes are expected due to varying requirements or external factors. By identifying these points and isolating them into separate components, you can make your software more flexible and easier to maintain.
For example:
```cpp
// Before isolation
class Document {
public:
void exportToJSON() { /* complex logic */ }
};
// After refactoring with a variation point
class JSONComponent {
public:
virtual void serialize(Document& doc) = 0;
};
class DefaultJSON : public JSONComponent {
public:
void serialize(Document& doc) override { /* simplified serialization */ }
