// Custom drawing logic for circles
}
void draw(const Square& square, /*some arguments*/) const override {
// Custom drawing logic for squares
}
};
```

:m The DrawStrategy pattern enables flexible drawing behaviors by allowing different strategies to be injected at runtime. This means you can easily switch between different drawing methods without changing the Shape classes directly. Each shape (Circle, Square) holds a unique_ptr to its specific DrawStrategy implementation.
