delete[] p; // Custom array deleter
});
```
This flexibility shows how policy-based design can be applied to manage resources differently.

:m Using multiple `std::unique_ptr` strategies can lead to larger object sizes due to pointer indirection, which can affect performance. Additionally, you lose the flexibility to change strategies at runtime and might end up with many different classes instead of a single one.
For example:
```cpp
