This approach can be inflexible because changes to the discount or tax logic would require modifying this single class. In contrast, using a decorator pattern allows for flexible combinations of different modifiers.

:m The primary goal of using the Decorator design pattern for price modifiers is to enable flexible and dynamic addition of functionalities such as discounts and taxes without modifying the core Item implementation. This approach promotes modularity, ease of extension, and adherence to the Open-Closed Principle (OCP).
For example:
