:m The `Item` class handles `dueDate` by wrapping it in an `Optional<LocalDate>` object, allowing it to represent a potentially missing due date.
```java
static class Item {
String name;
Optional<LocalDate> dueDate;
Item(String name) { this(name, null); }
Item(String name, LocalDate dueDate) { this.name = name; this.dueDate = (dueDate == null) ? Optional.empty() : Optional.of(dueDate); }
}
```

:m Key takeaways include understanding how to use enums for fixed sets of constants, and how to handle potentially missing values using the `Optional` class. These techniques help prevent NullPointerExceptions and make code more robust and readable.
