:m The `extends` keyword indicates that one interface is a subset of another, meaning every value of the derived interface must satisfy all the constraints defined in the base interface. This can include both adding new properties and modifying existing ones to match stricter types.
```typescript
interface Person { name: string; }
interface PersonSpan extends Person {
birth: Date;
death?: Date;
}
// A PersonSpan must have a `name` property, but may or may not have a `death` property.
```
