:m Discounting-aware importance sampling leverages the structure of returns as sums of discounted rewards. For each time step, only the first term in the product is used to scale the return, while the subsequent terms are ignored because they do not affect the final value.
Example: If an episode lasts 100 steps and \( \gamma = 0 \), the return from time 0 will be just \( G_0 = R_1 \). Its importance sampling ratio will be scaled by \( \pi(A_0|S_0) b(A_0|S_0) \), ignoring the other terms since they are independent and have an expected value of 1.
