:m Q-learning is an off-policy method that aims to find the optimal policy while learning the optimal action-value function without following it directly. It updates \( Q \) values based on the maximum expected future reward, regardless of the actions actually taken. On the other hand, Sarsa is on-policy and follows the current policy during both exploration and exploitation.
