:m Controlling variance is critical because importance sampling often involves products of policy ratios that are highly variable. These ratios can be very high or zero, and since they multiply the step size in SGD methods, this leads to large and unpredictable steps. Such steps can cause the parameter updates to take the algorithm to regions with different gradients, making the learning process unreliable.
