:m The Tree Backup algorithm works by using a tree structure to backpropagate returns from the end of an episode to the start, effectively computing the target values for off-policy learning in a way that avoids the use of importance sampling. This method stabilizes the updates and can lead to more reliable learning.
```java
// Pseudocode for Tree Backup algorithm
function treeBackup(node) {
if (node is terminal) {
return reward;
} else {
value = 0;
for each child node {
value += probability(child) * treeBackup(child);
}
return value + discountFactor * targetPolicyActionValue;
}
}
```

