:m Multipartite graphs are a type of graph where the nodes can be divided into two or more disjoint sets such that no edge connects nodes within the same set, but only links nodes from different sets. Bipartite graphs are the simplest form (two types of nodes), while tripartite and k-partite graphs involve three or more node types respectively.
