:m ETL involves extracting data from sources, transforming it through validation and normalization, and then loading it into a destination system. In contrast, ELT extracts data first, loads it directly into the target system, and performs transformation within that system. The choice depends on whether extensive transformation is needed before loading or can be handled in the target environment.
