:m Streams capture individual changes to the relation over time, whereas tables provide a snapshot of the entire relation at a specific point in time. The stream rendering is more concise as it captures only the delta of changes between each snapshot, while the sequence-of-tables TVR rendering provides clarity by showing the evolution of the relation over time.
