:m In a null-recurrent Markov chain, which is ergodic (aperiodic and irreducible), all states have zero limiting probability. This means that over an infinite time horizon, the system does not tend to spend any significant fraction of time in any particular state.
The mean return time to each state being infinite implies:
\[
\lim_{n \to \infty} P^n_{ij} = 0 \quad \text{for all states } i \text{ and } j
\]
Thus, there is no stationary distribution for a null-recurrent chain since the limiting probabilities sum to zero.
