:m Mr. Max, the largest job with size \(x = 10^{10}\), prefers SRPT over PS in expectation. Despite large jobs being ignored under SRPT until they start receiving service, once they begin to receive service, they gain priority over other jobs. This ensures that even the largest job will have a period of high priority.
```java
public class MaxJobPreference {
public double psPerformance(double x) {
// Simulate PS performance for a large job size x
return 100.0 / (x + 1);
}
public double srptPerformance(double x) {
