}
}
```

:m The All-Can-Win theorem holds because even large jobs prefer SRPT to PS in expectation. While large jobs are ignored under SRPT until they start receiving service, once they begin to receive service, their priority increases significantly. This ensures that every job, regardless of size, benefits more from SRPT than PS when the load is less than 1/2.
```java
