:m A watchdog is a background thread that monitors the health of a process. If any monitored metric breaches a configured threshold, the watchdog restarts the process. This mechanism helps maintain system reliability by automatically handling temporary issues and providing self-healing capabilities.
```java
public class Watchdog {
private int memThreshold = 80; // Memory usage percentage threshold
public void run() {
while (true) {
if (!checkHealth()) {
restartProcess();
}
try {
Thread.sleep(60000); // Sleep for 1 minute
} catch (InterruptedException e) {
Thread.currentThread().interrupt();
}
