:m Observability enables developers to understand the internal behavior of a system by observing its external interactions and outputs. By using traces and logs, developers can trace requests through various services and pinpoint issues that might not be immediately visible.
Example of tracing with Zipkin:
```java
public class ExampleService {
private final ZipkinTracer tracer;
public void processRequest(Request request) {
Span span = tracer.newSpan();
try (Scope scope = tracer.withSpan(span)) {
// Process the request
} catch (Exception e) {
span.addAnnotation("Error processing request");
span.error(e);
}
tracer.reporter().report(span);
}
}
```

